Subject: [PATCH] http: close the connection when the tuner cannot start

In --http mode, when tune() fails (the channel does not lock, the device
cannot be opened, the channel is unknown), recpt1 goes back to accept()
without closing the client's socket.  Each such request leaks one
descriptor, and the client gets "200 OK" and then nothing.  When the
descriptors run out, accept() fails with EMFILE and the daemon exits:
every later client gets "connection refused" until it is started again.

Close the socket before waiting for the next client.

---
diff --git a/recpt1/recpt1.c b/recpt1/recpt1.c
index 0cbbf3b..99f0903 100644
--- a/recpt1/recpt1.c
+++ b/recpt1/recpt1.c
@@ -924,6 +924,7 @@ main(int argc, char **argv)
             //tune
             if(tune(channel, &tdata, device) != 0){
                 fprintf(stderr, "Tuner cannot start recording\n");
+                close(connected_socket);
                 continue;
             }
         }else{    // -http-server add
